  "raw": {
    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Assistant-Professor--Pharmacy-Practice_R005215": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Pharmacy Practice",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: Regis University School of Pharmacy (RUSOP) invites applications at the Assistant Professor rank for a full-time, 12-month appointment in the Department of Pharmacy Practice. Regis seeks applicants with strong inpatient clinical pharmacy experience with expertise in oncology, internal medicine, critical care, or healthcare ethics and pharmacy law. The position provides an exciting opportunity to contribute to an innovative student-centered Doctor of Pharmacy program that integrates the biomedical, pharmaceutical, social administrative, and clinical sciences. Curricular content is developed primarily using Team-Based Learning™ (TBL), an active learning teaching model in which the faculty facilitates student learning that promotes self-directed learning, teamwork, and critical thinking skills. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include, but are not limited to, delivering curricular content in pharmacotherapy and laboratory courses, maintaining an innovative practice site providing patient care services and precepting IPPE/APPE students, as well as engaging in service to the school, college, university, and community while maintaining a scholarly agenda. Regis University is a nationally recognized Jesuit Catholic university located in the heart of Denver, Colorado. Regis University is comprised of three colleges including the Rueckert-Hartman College for Health Professions (RHCHP) which houses the School of Pharmacy. RHCHP includes the following programs: Division of Counseling and Family Therapy, Loretto Heights School of Nursing, and the School of Physical Therapy. This offers excellent opportunities for both collaboration and interprofessional education.   RUSOP has a traditional 4-year PharmD pathway and an accelerated 3-year PharmD pathway. RUSOP is a leader in active learning, combining our highly integrated curriculum with a team-taught approach via TBL. RUSOP provides a collaborative learning environment that prepares students to become an integral part of a health care team with access to hands-on opportunities via laboratory skills development, patient simulation, and experiential education. Regis emphasizes excellent teaching, values-based education, clinical expertise, service learning, and scholarship. The School of Pharmacy has been fully accredited by the Accreditation Council for Pharmacy Education since 2013 with most recent renewal in 2019. In addition, the School of Pharmacy has overall program averages for both the NAPLEX and postgraduate residency placement exceeding the national average. This faculty role directly supports Regis University’s strategic plan and Jesuit mission by fostering academic excellence, promoting compassionate service, and preparing students to become socially responsible health care professionals. Through a commitment to active learning, interprofessional collaboration, and community engagement, the Assistant Professor in Pharmacy Practice will play a key role in advancing health equity and developing future leaders in pharmacy who are guided by ethical reflection, lifelong learning, and service to others. Teaching: Develop instructional materials, assessments, and innovative teaching strategies to enhance student learning. Evaluate student performance through assessments and continuous feedback. Deliver and facilitate learning sessions in pharmacotherapy and skills-based learning courses. Clinical Practice and Precepting: Establish and maintain a clinical pharmacy practice site in an inpatient setting. Provide patient care services. Precept pharmacy students during clinical rotations to meet programmatic outcomes. Scholarship: Establish and maintain a scholarly agenda. Collaborate with faculty, clinicians, and students on research projects and publications. Pursue internal and external funding opportunities to support scholarly agenda.   Service: Contribute service to the School, College, University, Profession, and Community. Engage in professional organizations and maintain licensure and certifications relevant to practice. Working Conditions: Monday-Friday, approximately 8:30am - 5:00pm Occasional evening or weekend hours may be required for meetings, events, or additional responsibilities as assigned. Primary Work Location: Main NW Denver Campus Requires standing for extended periods during classroom or laboratory instruction. Clinical Site Location: based on expertise Qualifications: Education Pharm.D. (or equivalent) with Residency or Fellowship Training or Clinical Practice Experience (or equivalent) required. Completion of PGY2 residency training or completion of PGY1 pharmacy residency training with additional pharmacy practice experience. Licenses or Certifications Licensed or eligible for licensure to practice as a pharmacist in the state of Colorado. Professional Pharmacy Board Certification (or eligible for Board Certification) preferred. Experience Prior experience with course design, instruction, and evaluation preferred. Prior experience in teaching in an interdisciplinary and integrated curriculum preferred. Special knowledge, skills, abilities Strong interpersonal skills with excellent verbal and written communication required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, including Excel, Word, and Outlook, with the ability to efficiently manage documents, analyze data, and communicate effectively via email preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit your CV, cover letter and list of references with your application. Current employees, please submit an application by logging into Workday. Click on the Career Worklet and access the internal site. This position will remain open until filled with a priority application deadline of September 8th, 2026. Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: $102,000 - $105,000 /annually, commensurate with qualifications Application Deadline:"
    },
    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Marketing_R005363": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: The Anderson College of Business and Computing at Regis University in Denver, Colorado invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Marketing (tenure-track) position to begin in Fall of 2027. Qualified candidates will have earned a Ph.D. or DBA in Marketing (from an AACSB-accredited business school) or a related field by August of 2027 to be considered. The Anderson College seeks innovative, forward-thinking faculty who show potential for excellent teaching and outstanding research and scholarship. In line with our Jesuit history and values, we are particularly interested in candidates conducting research in the areas of Transformative Consumer Research (TCR), public policy, social justice, and/or environmental sustainability. Successful applicants should be able to translate their research interests into innovative courses, and they should also be able to teach across the spectrum of marketing classes including Principles of Marketing, Consumer Behavior, Marketing Research, Advertising and Promotion, International Marketing, Value Chain Management, Sales, and Digital Marketing. Major Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to teach five to seven graduate and/or undergraduate classes in their discipline based on the needs of various programs. The modalities may vary—in-person, online asynchronous, or hybrid—depending on the course, but it is expected that the candidate will primarily teach on campus. Conduct high-quality research and publish in peer-reviewed ranked journals. Perform service for the department, college, and university, including serving on committees. Advise students around course registration needs Qualifications: A PhD in Marketing (from an AACSB-accredited business school) or a related field Demonstrated ability to design, develop, and teach marketing courses Demonstrated potential to publish in quality peer-reviewed journals Please note that applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Regis University is unable to sponsor employment visas for this position. Start-Date: August 1, 2027 Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit a resume, cover letter, teaching statement, research statement a nd a list of 3 references with your application. Current employees, please submit an application with an updated cover letter and resume by logging into Workday. Click on the Jobs Hub Worklet to access the internal site.   For full consideration, apply by August 31, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Background and Context The Anderson College of Business and Computing was founded in 2020 to prepare students for a complex and ever-changing world that is increasingly blending business and technology. Founded on systems thinking, the College’s innovative curriculum develops graduates who are omni-skilled, resilient, and ready to contribute to a more flourishing world. At Regis University, we affirm our commitment to cultivating an inclusive, welcoming community grounded in Jesuit values and respect for the dignity of every person. Guided by cura personalis , we honor the whole person and recognize that our shared life is enriched by diverse perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. In the spirit of the Universal Apostolic Preferences, we strive to walk with those who are marginalized, journey alongside students and colleagues in formation, and act with care for our common home. We seek individuals who are committed to justice, dialogue, and mutual respect, and who will contribute to a community rooted in belonging, compassion, and the common good. For more information regarding the position please contact: Matt Daly, Associate Dean, Professor of Accounting mdaly@regis.edu or Abby Schneider, Ph.D., Professor and Program Director of Marketing aschneider@regis.edu Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: $75,000-$80,000 / annually, commensurate with qualifications Application Deadline: Post Internally and Externally"
    },
    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Assistant-Professor--Spanish_R005316": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Spanish",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: The Department of Modern Languages invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Spanish. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student mentorship, and scholarly activity. The faculty member will support the institution's mission and foster an inclusive learning environment that promotes intercultural competence, critical thinking, and effective communication. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Develop instructional plans (syllabus) for each class and ensure course content aligns with department standards; Teach Introduction and Intermediate Spanish classes to non-majors; Teach upper-division Spanish classes, and contribute a class to the integrative core curriculum; Grade assignments, papers, and other student work, monitor student progress, and provide additional guidance or instruction, where appropriate; Maintain office hours and occasionally meet with students outside office hours to support student learning;  Advise students Maintain currency in Spanish, and related disciplines, including occasional related conference attendance; Develop and continue scholarly research in the field, which may include the involvement of undergraduate students; Produce publications and/or conference presentations; Attend Regis College Faculty-Senate Forum Meeting attendance; 1-3 meetings per semester Attend Department of meetings in Modern and Classical Languages; Perform community or academic service outside the Department on committees, groups and/or task forces; Research focus in areas such as Spanish in the U.S., language variation and research with indigenous communities, languages in contact, sociolinguistics, and/or heritage language pedagogy and the use of AI. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Spanish, Applied Linguistics, or a closely related field 12 months experience teaching Spanish at an institute of higher education. Demonstrated working knowledge of: teaching Spanish for heritage speakers; research in second language acquisition, teacher training, language program development, language assessment, language and technology, and Sociolinguistics; and grant writing Minimum of 4 peer-reviewed publications in field of linguistics. Bilingual in English and Spanish, including Spanish heritage language acquisition Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit a resume, cover letter and list of references with your application. Current employees, please submit an application by logging into Workday. Click on the Career Worklet and access the internal site. Please ensure your application materials are complete by August 30th, 2026. Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: $71,017 annually Application Deadline:"
    },
    "https://regis.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Northwest-Denver-Campus/Pediatric-Nursing-Faculty_R005237": {
      "title": "Pediatric Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWorking at Regis University As Regis employees, we embrace our Jesuit Catholic values of respect, inclusion and equity, and welcome employees, faculty and students from all faiths and cultures. Together, we perform our duties in alignment with the mission of the University and seek dedicated individuals to contribute to and strengthen that mission and our service to students. Why Work at Regis? Job Summary: The Nursing Faculty is a member of the University who has been appointed to one of four academic ranks: Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. The faculty member will contribute to the academic, professional, and personal formation of nursing students through a combination of teaching, scholarship, and service. This role includes delivering high-quality instruction in classroom, online, and clinical settings; developing curriculum; evaluating student learning; and mentoring students. The faculty member collaborates with colleagues to design and implement innovative teaching strategies and assessments, including flipped classrooms, case studies, and competency-based evaluation. Clinical and laboratory oversight ensures students are well-prepared to provide compassionate, evidence-based care in diverse healthcare settings. Additionally, faculty advise students on academic planning, study skills, and testing strategies to support their academic success and holistic development. Major Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching:  Classroom, online, synchronous platforms   Curriculum planning and evaluation     Evaluation of student learning (grading, coaching, mentoring, evaluating)     Course planning with teaching team to include teaching strategies (lecture, flipped classroom, case studies), tests, competencies     Laboratory and clinical planning, supervision, evaluation, and oversight     Student academic advising, to include study skills, testing strategies, course planning     Clinical Supervision, including student and preceptor meetings, evaluation of assignments, community team building     Scholarship    Boyer’s model of scholarship: Teaching, Discovery, Integration, Application     Development and dissemination of nursing knowledge (posters, presentations, publication)     Ongoing personal and professional education and development     Service to institution, profession, community     Clinical/Professional practice     Service learning activities with students     Participation in school, college, and university committees and task forces     Participation in recruitment and retention activities at the school, college, and university level     Service to the profession at local, state, or national level     Working Conditions: Ranked faculty are hired on variable FTE Faculty Contract.  Holiday and leave vary according to FTE.  All leave (unpaid, professional, and service) is planned with the School in order to ensure effective year-round operation of the School’s nursing education programs. Workplace settings include classroom, office, skills and simulation laboratories, clinical settings, and community settings, including indoor and outdoor areas.  Qualifications: Education     A graduate degree in Nursing required.    Doctoral degree in nursing preferred. Licenses or Certifications     An active license in good standing to practice as a registered nurse in Colorado. Effective July 1, 2007, an active license in good standing includes registered nurses practicing pursuant to the terms and condition of the nurse licensure compact and the requirements set for in the state of Colorado Department of Regulatory Agencies, Division of Registration, Board of Nursing, Chapter II Rules and Regulations for Approval of Nursing Education Programs.  Nurse Practitioners must be board certified in the appropriate specialty and hold a Colorado APRN license.  Nurse Practitioners engaged in faculty practice must have a Colorado APRN license and prescriptive authority for the designated population foci Experience     A minimum of two years of full-time, or equivalent, professional nursing clinical experience     Documented knowledge and skills related to the teaching of adults, teaching methodology, curriculum development and evaluation Special knowledge, skills, abilities     Knowledge of leadership and team building  Use Microsoft Windows, Microsoft Office, Web-browser, personal information management software, advising, and information management software  Work to deadline  Outstanding oral and written communication skills  Demonstrated organizational skills  Project planning and priority setting capabilities       Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit your CV, cover letter and list of references with your application. Current employees, please submit an application by logging into Workday. Click on the Career Worklet and access the internal site. This position will remain open until filled with a priority application deadline of June 15th, 2026. Regis University offers a broad range of benefits that includes: Comprehensive group health insurance, including medical, dental, vision, disability and life insurance. A generous tuition benefit for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Mission leave to allow our employees to engage in acts of service or to have time for personal reflection. The \"Gift of Time\" when Regis closes between Christmas Day and New Year's Day. Options for flexible work arrangements based on position. You can learn more about our benefits by clicking the links below. 26-27 Employee Benefits Summary or https://www.regis.edu/_documents/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/regis-university-employee-benefits-guide.pdf Pay Rate: Salary dependent on faculty rank. Instructor $56,500 - $75,300, Assistant Professor $63,300- $84,400, Associate Professor $66,300- $90,000/annually, commensurate with qualifications Application Deadline: Post Internally and Externally"
    },
